  "chapter": {
    "number": 94,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(95) The praise of a Song by David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Come, let us exult",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 186
          },
          {
            "text": "in the Lord; let us make a joyful noise to God our Saviour.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let us come before his presence with thanksgiving, and make a joyful noise to him with psalms.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the Lord is a great God, and a great king over all gods:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 187
          },
          {
            "text": "for the Lord will not cast off his people.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the ends of the earth are in his hands; and the heights of the mountains are his.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the sea is his, and he made it: and his hands formed the dry land.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Come, let us worship and fall down before him; and weep before the Lord that made us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he is our God; and we are the people of his pasture, and the sheep of his hand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "To-day, if you⌃ will hear his voice, harden not your hearts, as in the provocation, according to the day of",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 188
          },
          {
            "text": "irritation in the wilderness:",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "where your fathers tempted me, proved me, and saw my works.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Forty years was I grieved with this generation, and said, They do always err in their heart, and they have not known my ways.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So I swore in my wrath, They shall not enter into my rest.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 186,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. to.",
